  "id": "geriatric-rehabilitation",
  "term": "geriatric rehabilitation",
  "definition": "Geriatric rehabilitation is a structured, multi-professional rehabilitation approach for older inpatients, often provided after an acute health event or alongside acute hospital care. It uses multidimensional assessment and therapy to help people with multiple health conditions maintain or regain functional independence, including physical and cognitive abilities, in line with the person’s own goals.",
